 ENDF/B-VI MOD 2 Evaluation, September 1992, P.G. Young (LANL)     725 1451
                                                                   725 1451
 Extension to 40 MeV                                               725 1451
     The modified version of the ENDF/B-VI evaluation created for  725 1451
 DNA (described below) is extended in energy to 40 MeV. This ext-  725 1451
 tension was accomplished using experimental data and the 9/92     725 1451
 Version of the GNASH code, which was updated for higher energy    725 1451
 calculations. More details will be given in a later progress      725 1451
 report.                                                           725 1451
     The ENDF/B-VI evaluation was modified for DNA use to include  725 1451
 results from Hale's R-matrix analysis that include Harvey's new   725 1451
 total cross section measurement. These results are interim until  725 1451
 we can incorporate the new ORNL scattering data. The ORNL         725 1451
 preliminary scattering results confirm the parity of the first    725 1451
 resonance as being positive, as used in the R-matrix analysis.    725 1451
                                                                   725 1451
