 MT=1  Total Cross Section                                         725 1451
   Zero to 2.2 MeV, SIGT is obtained from sum of elastic, (n,p0),  725 1451
     (n,a0) cross sections from r-matrix analysis, plus the (n,g)  725 1451
     cross section described below. The coupled-channel r-matrix   725 1451
     analysis was performed with the EDA code, fitting simultane-  725 1451
     ously almost all available total, (n,n), (n,p0), and (n,a0)   725 1451
     exp. data.  The most important total cross section used were  725 1451
     [Me49,Bi59,Bi69] at lower energies, and [Ca70,He70,Fo71]      725 1451
     at higher energies. Significant shape difference found in     725 1451
     the 0.1 - 20 keV region as compared to ENDF/B-V.              725 1451
   2.2 MeV to 20 MeV, from [Ca70,He70,Fo71] using Ca70 alone       725 1451
     at sharp resonances. Smoothed by appropriate fits, log-log    725 1451
     interpolations is good to 1.3 pct to 0.4 MeV, linear inter-   725 1451
     polation is good to 0.5 pct from 0.4 to 20 MeV, absolute      725 1451
     error less than 1 pct above 2.2 MeV. Minor changes made in    725 1451
     ENDF/V.2 evaluation in certain regions of high structure.     725 1451
